      "title": "Chris Van Hollen to challenge Chuck Schumer for Senate majority leader",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/12/chris-van-hollen-chuck-schumer-senate-majority-leader",
      "description": "<p>Maryland Democrat challenges party leader after midterms sweep, saying: ‘The American people called for change’</p><p>Chris Van Hollen, the Democratic senator of Maryland, announced on Thursday that he is challenging Chuck Schumer for the role of Senate majority leader when <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/democrats\">Democrats</a> regain the chamber’s majority in January.</p><p>“In this election, the American people called for change. They called for a change from Donald Trump’s disastrous policies – but even bigger than that, a change from the status quo that isn’t working for working people,” Van Hollen said in <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DfqhAF9nfio/?hl=en\">a statement</a> posted on social media.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/12/chris-van-hollen-chuck-schumer-senate-majority-leader\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-13T02:30:07"
    },
